# RopeTool.Mod's own insert clamps a negative pos to the start
# (Ropes.Mod's Insert itself clamps); rope_tool's BEFORE is Positive, so
# "-5" is not a representable index at all rather than a differently-
# handled one -- Positive'Value ("-5") itself raises Constraint_Error
# before Ropes.Insert is ever called. "--" still lets the leading "-"
# of -5 through as a plain argument instead of being read as an
# option, same as the Oberon original (confirmed against a real run:
# Arg_Parser supports "--" the same way ArgParser does).
program rope_tool
arg insert
arg hello world
arg --
arg -5
arg X
status 1
output
Error: not a valid index: "-5"
